    <briefdescription>
<para>Soft-CS SPI slave on a shared <ref refid="classStmSpiBus" kindref="compound">StmSpiBus</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Owns one GPIO chip-select and a per-device SPI mode (<ref refid="structhf__spi__device__config__t_1a7f5737b1045c78fc5ed7d8f2b6c9c0cf" kindref="member">hf_spi_device_config_t::mode</ref>). Each Transfer:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Takes <ref refid="classStmSpiBusLock" kindref="compound">StmSpiBusLock</ref> (RTOS mutex — peers wait),</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Parks <bold>all</bold> soft-CS on the bus idle-high,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Applies this device&apos;s CPOL/CPHA (SPE toggle only with every CS high),</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Flushes the RX FIFO,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Scopes <bold>only this</bold> CS with <ref refid="classSoftChipSelectGuard" kindref="compound">SoftChipSelectGuard</ref>,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Releases the bus lock.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Mixed Mode 0/1/3 slaves may share one CubeMX SPI peripheral. Chip handlers and external drivers must not poke CS — only <ref refid="classStmSpiDevice_1aac96933b7c2db6fa0e675ee472e91ec5" kindref="member">Transfer</ref> / <ref refid="classStmSpiDevice_1a0460008b43be1249a3268280b877c7b1" kindref="member">TransferChain</ref>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>CS low during a Mode1 (TLE) frame is expected. CS must be high for every other slave while Mode0/1/3 SPE/CPOL is being rewritten. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
